        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\sqrt{5\\sqrt6+12}=\\sqrt[4]{54}+\\sqrt[4]{24}$.\n\nMultiply the result of part (a) by $\\sqrt[4]6$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\sqrt{5\\sqrt6+12}&=\\sqrt{\\sqrt6(5+2\\sqrt6)}\\\\\\sqrt{5\\sqrt6+12}&=\\sqrt[4]6\\,\\sqrt{5+2\\sqrt6}\\\\\\sqrt{5\\sqrt6+12}&=\\sqrt[4]6(\\sqrt3+\\sqrt2)\\\\\\sqrt{5\\sqrt6+12}&=\\sqrt[4]6\\,\\sqrt[4]9+\\sqrt[4]6\\,\\sqrt[4]4\\\\\\sqrt{5\\sqrt6+12}&=\\sqrt[4]{54}+\\sqrt[4]{24}.\\end{align*}$$",
